  {
   "id": "nJ1KZSaow78J",
   "from": "Andy Kipp",
   "author": "e84e7628b5f8a3e1",
   "date": "2014-06-23T15:11:44Z",
   "subject": "Re: [shinyapps-users] Errror using deployApp()",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Folks,<div><br></div><div>I apologize this error message is a little confusing. What it is saying here is that your application name in invalid. Application names must be at least 3 characters, and may NOT contain spaces. . By default application names are the name of the directory you are deploying. To work around this, you can either a) rename your application directory, or b) call <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">deployApp(appName=&quot;my-app-name&quot;)</font></div>\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div>Hope that helps.</div><div><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">-Andy</font></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Sun, Jun 22, 2014 at 2:09 PM, Tareef Kawaf <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tar...@rstudio.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n\r\n</div></div>"
